course: dictionary
lesson: 13975
title: Lob
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lob can be a verb or a noun. Its main meaning is to throw or hit something high in the air, in a slow curve. «She lobbed the ball over the fence.» The clues are high and over: the ball goes up and comes down on the other side, so lob means a high, curving throw or shot.
explain: In sport, a lob is a high shot that goes over an opponent's head. «The striker lobbed the ball over the goalkeeper and it dropped into the net.» The goalkeeper could not reach it because it went over them. You will meet this word in tennis and football.
explain: Lob has other meanings too. In informal British and Australian speech, to lob something is to throw it carelessly: «Lob it in the bin.» In informal Australian and New Zealand speech, to lob in means to arrive, often unexpectedly: «He lobbed in at midnight.» Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: Lob is a verb and a noun: you can lob something, or hit a lob.
fact: «Lob» means to throw or hit something high in the air, in a slow curve.
fact: In tennis and football, a lob is a high shot over an opponent's head.
fact: In science lessons, the curve of a lobbed ball is called a parabola.
fact: Informally, «lob» can mean to throw something carelessly (UK and Australia), or to arrive unexpectedly (Australia and New Zealand).
exercise: «The keeper was off his line, so Mia lobbed the ball over him.» What does lobbed mean here? | Dropped it at her feet | Kicked very hard along the ground | *Hit high over the keeper's head | Ran past him quickly
exercise: Sam shouts, «Lob it here!» in the playground. What does he mean? | Break it into pieces | Run away with it | *Throw it to me | Hide it from me
exercise: «He lobbed in at midnight, long after everyone had gone to bed.» What does lobbed in mean? | Shouted loudly | Fell fast asleep | Left in a hurry | *Arrived, often unexpectedly
test: In a science lesson, the curve of a lobbed ball is called what? | Square | *Parabola | Circle | Straight line
test: In «She played a lovely lob over the net», what kind of word is lob? | Adverb | Adjective | Verb | *Noun
exam: «The bin was full, so Ravi lobbed the empty crisp packet across the room.» What does lobbed mean here? | Measured it with a ruler | *Threw it carelessly | Carefully placed it on a shelf | Gently wrapped it up
